-- title:
--   A rational point of exact order $25$ gives a rational noncusp on $X_1(25)$
-- statement:
--   Let $E/ℚ$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve and let $x∈E(ℚ)$ be a rational torsion point of additive order exactly $25$. Then there exists a degree-one place $P$ of the level-$25$ modular function field such that $P$ is not a cusp: $$deg(P)=1,\qquad P\notin Cusps(X_1(25)).$$ This is the bridge from a hypothetical elliptic-curve torsion point to the rational place contradicted by the endgame.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

